Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: Distinguish an unspecified clock wait from a read error

UFS devices may return 00h for an undefined bRefClkGatingWaitTime.
A successful query with that value still needs the conservative default
but it is not a query error. Keep a warning with the selected delay and
preserve the error and return status of a failed query. Assign the fallback
explicitly on failure instead of relying on the output of the query.

Found on WDC SDINEDK4-256G 1088 in Xiaomi Umi. The 255 us default and the
clock gating policy are unchanged.

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
index 572c0510d..e4adb9cd9 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -3899,14 +3899,15 @@ static int ufshcd_get_ref_clk_gating_wait(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 		err = ufshcd_query_attr_retry(hba, UPIU_QUERY_OPCODE_READ_ATTR,
 				QUERY_ATTR_IDN_REF_CLK_GATING_WAIT_TIME, 0, 0,
 				&gating_wait);
-		if (err)
+		if (err) {
+			gating_wait = UFSHCD_REF_CLK_GATING_WAIT_US;
 			dev_err(hba->dev, "Failed reading bRefClkGatingWait. err = %d, use default %uus\n",
-					 err, gating_wait);
-
-		if (gating_wait == 0) {
+				err, gating_wait);
+		} else if (!gating_wait) {
+			/* A successful read can return zero (no timing specified). */
 			gating_wait = UFSHCD_REF_CLK_GATING_WAIT_US;
-			dev_err(hba->dev, "Undefined ref clk gating wait time, use default %uus\n",
-					 gating_wait);
+			dev_warn(hba->dev, "Undefined ref clk gating wait time, use default %uus\n",
+				 gating_wait);
 		}
 
 		hba->dev_info.clk_gating_wait_us = gating_wait;
